[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189992635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3189992635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3189992635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-I2y7","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T22:07:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-14T22:08:21Z","body":"Remember to check the freelook navigation scheme settings too: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e67074d0abe9b69f3d1944293342f0664e34c946/editor/scene/3d/node_3d_editor_plugin.cpp#L239-L248\r\n\r\nI would prefer keeping <kbd>Q</kbd>/<kbd>E</kbd> as-is, but I'm OK with introducing <kbd>R</kbd>/<kbd>F</kbd> for global up/down instead. Ideally, I would use <kbd>Space</kbd>/<kbd>Shift</kbd> for global up/down (matching Minecraft creative behavior), but we already use <kbd>Shift</kbd> as a speed modifier. Maybe <kbd>Space</kbd>/<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>, but <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> is a key you often press (e.g. to toggle snapping).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3189992635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3190228059","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3190228059","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3190228059,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-JwRb","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-14T23:54:18Z","updated_at":"2025-08-15T00:54:50Z","body":"@Calinou I'm against adding R/F for global up/down because it defeats the purpose of unifying these controls across most 3D software. We could add Space/Ctrl to do this, though, that's a good idea. I don't think people use snapping while moving the camera, right? EDIT: PR updated.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3190228059/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432878661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3432878661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3432878661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MnZJF","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T15:06:20Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T15:06:20Z","body":"@passivestar @lander-vr I'd also appreciate your input on this PR in terms of UX :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3432878661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3433848009","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3433848009","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3433848009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MrFzJ","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T19:09:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T19:09:55Z","body":"I think this is fine, although you could have just 4 actions instead of 6:\r\n\r\n- `freelook_up` <kbd>E</kbd>\r\n- `freelook_down` <kbd>Q</kbd>\r\n- `freelook_up_alt_axis` <kbd>Space</kbd>\r\n- `freelook_down_alt_axis` <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>\r\n\r\nThe 2 new actions would also depend on `freelook_navigation_scheme` but move on the opposite axis between local/global. This approach would embrace the existence of `freelook_navigation_scheme` instead working around it with new local/global shortcuts. Another alternative would be to deprecate `freelook_navigation_scheme` and leave *only* explicit local/global shortcuts, but that would be a more intrusive change, not to mention that it also affects the `forward` vector and not just `up`, so that is probably not a good option\r\n\r\nIf you want to add `R/F` bindings by default to better match the expectations of users coming from other software you don't need extra actions for those either, you could just add them to the existing `freelook_up` and `freelook_down` actions alongside the already bound `Q/E`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3433848009/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3434791760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3434791760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3434791760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MusNQ","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T01:51:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T01:51:58Z","body":"@Calinou I updated the PR to fix Shift+F conflicting with the controls. Now, right-mouse-activated freelook allows users to press Shift and/or F without accidentally disabling freelook, and Shift+F without right mouse still works.\r\n\r\n@passivestar The idea is to provide R/F and Space/Ctrl as dedicated keys that always perform these functions, while E/Q are configurable. This way users can configure what they want E/Q to do, without affecting R/F. If R/F were bound to the same actions as E/Q, this ability would not exist.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3434791760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3435467951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3435467951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3435467951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MxRSv","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T07:09:22Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T07:09:22Z","body":"> This way users can configure what they want E/Q to do, without affecting R/F.\r\n\r\nDo you expect the user to need both dedicated and scheme-dependent keys at the same time while using the editor and to use those 6 different keys? The `navigation_scheme` setting will probably at most be only ever changed once when the user first downloads godot","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3435467951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3567130319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109598#issuecomment-3567130319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109598","id":3567130319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UnhbP","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-22T23:11:46Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T23:14:32Z","body":"@passivestar Yes, because the point is to give users the freedom regardless of whatever navigation scheme they have selected. It is perfectly valid to want to do a different style of up/down movement independent of the editor setting, so that both up/down behaviors are available regardless of how the users configure the WASDQE keys to behave\r\n\r\nAlso, more importantly, I want to have consistency between applications. Having these exist on separate keys (R/F and Space/Ctrl) allows users to always press those keys to always get that behavior regardless of application *and* configuration.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3567130319/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]